    "content_text": "Ravi Uppal, co-promoter of the multi-crore Mahadev online betting app, has been arrested in the UAE, and India is moving to extradite him, officials said on Wednesday (November 4, 2026).\nThe development follows the\nreturn from Oman\non November 1 of Mr. Uppal's friend and another Mahadev app promoter, Saurabh Chandrakar, after a court there allowed his extradition to India in a money-laundering case being probed by the Enforcement Directorate (ED).\nAuthorities in Dubai arrested a 46-year-old Uppal based on an Interpol Red Notice issued by Indian probe agencies, officials told\nPTI\n.\nThe Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI) and the ED are working to extradite him to India, they said.\nRavi Uppal was once detained by authorities in the UAE in 2023, but agencies later found that he was in Australia.\nProbe agencies have claimed that Mr. Uppal obtained a passport from Vanuatu, an archipelagic country located in the South Pacific Ocean, just like Chandrakar.\nIt charged Mr. Uppal in October 2023, stating that he \"generated and enjoyed proceeds of crime and is involved in their concealment and layering\".\nIt alleged Ravi Uppal was \"looking after the delivery of the liaisoning money to the bureaucrats and politicians of Chhattisgarh through Chandrabhushan Verma, an assistant sub-inspector of police, and some others\".\nBoth Mr. Uppal and Mr. Chandrakar hail from Bhilai town in Durg district of Chhattisgarh.\nA special court in Raipur on Wednesday (November 4, 2026) granted eight-day custody of Chandrakar to the CBI.\nThe agency said the Mahadev app, also called Mahadev Online Book (MOB), began operations in 2019-20. Its user base grew \"sharply\" during the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020 and continued to expand.\nThe app, which runs through thousands of panels, allegedly generated proceeds of crime worth ₹80,000 crore since 2019.\nPublished\n- November 05, 2026 07:01 am IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\